cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying dataset, please cite both the article and the archived release."
title: "QG-Python: a reproducible 1.5-layer quasi-geostrophic modelling service with spectral stability and filter sensitivity diagnostics"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-08-30
type: software
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22168803
url: "https://github.com/enino84/qg-leapfrog-stability"
repository-code: "https://github.com/enino84/qg-leapfrog-stability"
abstract: >-
  Open, reproducible Python implementation of the 1.5-layer
  quasi-geostrophic model originally distributed as QG-C, in which the
  Fortran multigrid Helmholtz solver is replaced by a direct sparse LU
  factorization. Exposes RK4, dp5 and Leapfrog with the Robert-Asselin
  and Robert-Asselin-Williams filters under a single API, together with
  diagnostic modules for the linearised operator, its eigenspectrum and
  the maximum Lyapunov exponent.
keywords:
  - quasi-geostrophic model
  - Leapfrog scheme
  - Robert-Asselin-Williams filter
  - stability analysis
  - Lyapunov exponent
  - reproducible geoscience software
